q16: `str.contains("MEDIUM POLISHED*")` is upstream's bug. As a regex, `D*`
matches zero or more D, so the filter is really contains("MEDIUM POLISHE");
the intent (and TPC-H's `p_type not like 'MEDIUM POLISHED%'`) is a prefix
match. Reported upstream, not fixed. Applied to every polars-benchmark
checkout that runs Ibex comparisons; bench_pdsh_engine.py records the
applied diff as `upstream_worktree_patch`.

diff --git a/queries/polars/q16.py b/queries/polars/q16.py
index a17c87d..bb739fd 100644
--- a/queries/polars/q16.py
+++ b/queries/polars/q16.py
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ def q(
     return (
         part.join(partsupp, left_on="p_partkey", right_on="ps_partkey")
         .filter(pl.col("p_brand") != var1)
-        .filter(pl.col("p_type").str.contains("MEDIUM POLISHED*").not_())
+        .filter(pl.col("p_type").str.starts_with("MEDIUM POLISHED").not_())
         .filter(pl.col("p_size").is_in([49, 14, 23, 45, 19, 3, 36, 9]))
         .join(supplier, left_on="ps_suppkey", right_on="s_suppkey", how="anti")
         .group_by("p_brand", "p_type", "p_size")
